  "limitations": [
    "single-process SessionRuntime fork and real signatures; synthetic authenticated peer transport, not native UID isolation",
    "mock source acquisition and pin liveness; no actual readCommitted/journal/checkpoint or use/ACK/finish path",
    "envelope counters cover only SessionServer-to-owner inner request verification; handshake/client/reply checks remain outside these counters",
    "owner payload validation, current local gates and distinct pre/post live checks remain",
    "H0 scaling is arithmetic using different saved executions, not a graph-read timing measurement; removed-work projection excludes new facts overhead and is not a worst-case CPU bound",
    "primary guard policy is shared across S*/A*, while intent digests intentionally differ by mode; no retry deadline/attempt reset",
    "registry immutability is a deep freeze and object identity inside this fork; the production session runtime has no such freeze, so adopting facts needs its own contract"
  ],
